  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1046 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nDRY WEATHER RETURNS:\n\nA quick, transitory ridge will build over the area today though\nsome high clouds will start infiltrating the region from west \nto east ahead of the next shortwave. As the wave moves through \non Friday, some very isolated showers may occur over the higher \nterrain with maybe some light snow at the highest elevations. Do\nnot anticipate any accumulations, maybe a light dusting, as the\nwave moves through. As we head towards the evening hours, \nclouds will lift from west to east. After that, high pressure \nbuilds back in Sunday and persists for much of next week. High \ntemperatures will start inching up above seasonal norms next \nweek. This will be welcome relief after all the rain and \nunsettled weather we've seen recently.",
